{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>My sin</b> — corresponding to 'covering of sin.'" "<b>And my iniquity</b> — corresponding to 'HaShem will not reckon to him iniquity and transgression'; <b>is forgiven</b> — corresponding to 'whose transgression is borne.'" "And the meaning of <b>I will acknowledge</b> — to confess." "And the meaning of <b>is forgiven</b> — by the Holy Spirit; or that his iniquity has been borne until this day."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:10.797985237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}